This software began as a fork of the Tasks Map plugin by Nico Klaassen
(https://github.com/NicoKNL/tasks-map) and has since been substantially
extended. Tasks Map is released under the MIT License, and its original
copyright notice is retained in LICENSE as that license requires.

The graph canvas, the dual inline/note task model, the Dataview integration
and the filtering core all began in that project. What has been added since
is described under "Relationship to Tasks Map" in README.md.

This file carries the attribution that previously sat inside LICENSE. It was
moved so that LICENSE holds the unmodified MIT text: licence detection
compares the file against a template and treats added prose as a
modification, which left the repository reading as unlicensed.
